Add explicit #include <algorithm> in source files that use std algorithms.

Under newer GCC (13+) and libc++ stacks, the <algorithm> header is no
longer transitively pulled in by other STL headers. Files that use
std::find / std::copy / std::max previously compiled by accident but
now fail with:

    error: 'find' is not a member of 'std'; did you mean 'bind'?

This affects all 5 files in the set that use std algorithms without
an explicit #include.

Upstream report / fix candidate: these are trivial one-line additions
at the top of each file; equivalent changes should be submitted to
3MFConsortium/lib3mf upstream.

